---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { AUTHOR_NAME, CONTACT_EMAIL, LAST_UPDATED, SITE_NAMES } from '../../data/site-config';
import { route } from '../../i18n/routes';
import { displayDate } from '../../lib/format';
const lang = 'en';
---
<PageLayout title={`Editorial policy of ${SITE_NAMES[lang]}: sources and corrections`} description="Which FINRA and NASAA documents Series Mock Exam relies on, how its practice questions are written, which sources it refuses and how a mistake is corrected and dated." lang={lang} noindex={true} breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Editorial policy' }]} showAuthor={false}>
  <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none">
    <h1>Editorial and corrections policy</h1>
    <p>People use these pages to decide when to sit an exam that costs up to a few hundred dollars and that can delay a job offer when failed. A stale fee or a wrong waiting period costs them money or weeks, so every figure points back to the official page it was read on.</p>
    <h2>Who is responsible</h2><p>{AUTHOR_NAME}, reachable at <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.</p>
    <h2>What we read</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>finra.org: the exam pages, the content outlines, the scheduling pages, FINRA Rules 1210, 1220, 1240 and 4210, the fee schedule and Regulatory Notices;</li>
      <li>nasaa.org: the study guides and test specifications of the Series 63, 65 and 66;</li>
      <li>federal texts for the exam math: Regulation T and the SEC's T+1 settlement rule.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>How the questions are written</h2><p>Each question takes one topic of an official outline and asks about it in our own words. We never copy a question from a prep provider, a book, a flash-card site or a real exam, and we never present our questions as real exam questions.</p>
    <h2>Sources we refuse</h2><p>Prep providers, course sellers, forums and flash-card sites never supply a figure here. Pass rates are not published, because FINRA and NASAA publish no current ones. A rule we cannot find on an official page is not published.</p>
    <h2>Review cycle</h2><p>Formats and fees are read again when FINRA publishes a new fee schedule, a new outline or a Regulatory Notice on qualification exams; announced changes are shown as coming, with their date, never as current.</p>
    <h2>Corrections</h2>
    <ol><li>We open the official page again.</li><li>We correct the parameter file or the question, and add an automated test for the case.</li><li>The site rebuilds and every page shows the new date.</li></ol>
    <h2>Independence</h2><p>No regulator, firm, prep provider or publisher pays for or reviews what is published here, and the site carries no affiliate link. See also the <a href={route('method', lang)}>method page</a>. Version of <time datetime={LAST_UPDATED}>{displayDate(LAST_UPDATED, 'en-US')}</time>.</p>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
